      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَافٌّ</span></b>  act. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفَّ</span> in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفَّ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">العَرُوسَ</span>: fem. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>: pl. of the latter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَوَافُّ</span>.
Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَحَفَتْ زَوَافُّهَا</span>, a phrase mentioned by Lh,
meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اللَّوَاتِىزَفَفْنَهَا</span> [i. e. <i>The women who
conducted her to her husband walked along gently</i>].
(TA.)

